### Events platform: REST Client file (VS Code extension "REST Client")
### Run the requests top to bottom. Requests marked "# @name x" save their response for later ones.
### Before starting: docker compose up -d ; npm run seed ; npm run dev
### Paste the ids printed by `npm run seed` below.

@host = http://localhost:3000
@admin = PASTE_ADMIN_ID
@alice = PASTE_ALICE_ID
@bob = PASTE_BOB_ID
@carol = PASTE_CAROL_ID
@dave = PASTE_DAVE_ID

### 1. Health -> {"status":"ok","db":"ok"}
GET {{host}}/health

### 2a. Create partner (admin)
# @name partner
POST {{host}}/partners
Content-Type: application/json
x-user-id: {{admin}}

{ "type": "cafe", "name": "Walkthrough Cafe", "city": "Mumbai", "capacity": 40 }

### 2b. List partners (filters)
GET {{host}}/partners?type=cafe&city=Mumbai

### 2c. Create event (draft). waitlist_fee is charged by the mock payment.
# @name event
POST {{host}}/events
Content-Type: application/json
x-user-id: {{admin}}

{
  "partner_id": "{{partner.response.body.id}}",
  "title": "Walkthrough Night",
  "description": "Created from requests.http",
  "starts_at": "2030-01-15T18:00:00+05:30",
  "capacity": 1,
  "waitlist_fee": 500,
  "needs_host": true
}

### 2d. Publish it
PATCH {{host}}/events/{{event.response.body.id}}/publish
x-user-id: {{admin}}

### 2e. List events -> partner_name / partner_city joined in, stats included
GET {{host}}/events

### 3a. User A (alice) joins the waitlist -> 201 with payment
# @name waitA
POST {{host}}/events/{{event.response.body.id}}/waitlist
x-user-id: {{alice}}

### 3b. User B (bob) joins the waitlist -> 201
# @name waitB
POST {{host}}/events/{{event.response.body.id}}/waitlist
x-user-id: {{bob}}

### 3c. A again -> 409
POST {{host}}/events/{{event.response.body.id}}/waitlist
x-user-id: {{alice}}

### 4a. Admin reviews the waitlist (profile + payment joined)
GET {{host}}/admin/events/{{event.response.body.id}}/waitlist?status=pending
x-user-id: {{admin}}

### 4b. Approve A -> 200 (capacity is 1)
PATCH {{host}}/admin/waitlist/{{waitA.response.body.id}}
Content-Type: application/json
x-user-id: {{admin}}

{ "status": "approved", "note": "Looks great" }

### 4c. Approve B -> 409 (event full)
PATCH {{host}}/admin/waitlist/{{waitB.response.body.id}}
Content-Type: application/json
x-user-id: {{admin}}

{ "status": "approved" }

### 4d. Reject B -> 200
PATCH {{host}}/admin/waitlist/{{waitB.response.body.id}}
Content-Type: application/json
x-user-id: {{admin}}

{ "status": "rejected", "note": "Profile incomplete" }

### 5a. C (carol) applies to host
# @name hostC
POST {{host}}/events/{{event.response.body.id}}/host-applications
Content-Type: application/json
x-user-id: {{carol}}

{ "pitch": "I run a board-game club" }

### 5b. D (dave) applies to host
POST {{host}}/events/{{event.response.body.id}}/host-applications
Content-Type: application/json
x-user-id: {{dave}}

{ "pitch": "I love hosting dinners" }

### 5c. Events needing a host -> host_applicant_count = 2
GET {{host}}/hosts/events

### 5d. Admin sees applicants with profiles
GET {{host}}/admin/events/{{event.response.body.id}}/host-applications
x-user-id: {{admin}}

### 5e. Approve C
PATCH {{host}}/admin/host-applications/{{hostC.response.body.id}}
Content-Type: application/json
x-user-id: {{admin}}

{ "status": "approved" }

### 5f. Event detail -> C listed under hosts
GET {{host}}/events/{{event.response.body.id}}

### 6a. A swipes right (interested)
PUT {{host}}/events/{{event.response.body.id}}/swipe
Content-Type: application/json
x-user-id: {{alice}}

{ "direction": "right" }

### 6b. B swipes left (skip)
PUT {{host}}/events/{{event.response.body.id}}/swipe
Content-Type: application/json
x-user-id: {{bob}}

{ "direction": "left" }

### 6c. Top events -> interest_count +1 (from A only)
GET {{host}}/events/top?limit=10

### 6d. Feed for A -> event gone
GET {{host}}/events/feed
x-user-id: {{alice}}

### 6e. Feed for B -> event gone
GET {{host}}/events/feed
x-user-id: {{bob}}

### 6f. Refresh rank scores, then re-check top ordering
POST {{host}}/admin/jobs/refresh-rank
x-user-id: {{admin}}

###
GET {{host}}/events/top

### 7a. Upload an image (put a real jpg/png at ./sample.jpg first). First image becomes the cover.
# @name upload
POST {{host}}/events/{{event.response.body.id}}/media
x-user-id: {{admin}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=XBOUNDARY

--XBOUNDARY
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="alt_text"

Cover photo
--XBOUNDARY
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="sample.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./sample.jpg
--XBOUNDARY--

### 7b. Open this URL in the browser to see the image (Ctrl+click it)
GET {{host}}/media/{{upload.response.body.media_id}}

### 7c. Events list returns cover_media_id only, no bytes
GET {{host}}/events

### 8a. Create a product with variants (admin)
POST {{host}}/products
Content-Type: application/json
x-user-id: {{admin}}

{
  "name": "Walkthrough Hoodie",
  "description": "Warm",
  "variants": [
    { "sku": "WALK-HOOD-M", "size": "M", "color": "grey", "price": 1999, "stock": 10 },
    { "sku": "WALK-HOOD-L", "size": "L", "color": "grey", "price": 1999, "stock": 5 }
  ]
}

### 8b. Products with variants nested
GET {{host}}/products

### 9. Audit log: no endpoint (not in the brief). Run this in PowerShell instead:
###   docker exec events_db psql -U events -d events -c "SELECT id, action, entity_type, actor_id, metadata, created_at FROM audit_log ORDER BY id"
